# `.hermes/` is instance-local runtime/session state for a deployed Creator
# Engine instance (live `STATE.md`, handoffs, tmux/pane facts, etc.). Upstream
# protocols and templates live under `docs/operations/` and `templates/`.
# Do not unignore `.hermes/`; do not commit live instance state upstream.
.hermes/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Claude Code local settings override (CC-G-C / D4). A gitignored local-override
# source must never be committed: it could silently weaken or disable the
# committed Ring 1 hook-pack. Governed launches also pin `--setting-sources
# project` to exclude `local`. See docs/operations/CLAUDE_CODE_HOOK_PACK.md.
.claude/settings.local.json

# G2.003.1 CE-event runtime instance state. `.ce/ce-events/spool/` is the
# local, generated append-only CE-event chain zone the `ce event` runtime writes
# (head manifests + per-block files). It is instance-local runtime state, never
# tracked. This is a minimal, additive instance-zone line: do NOT wholesale-
# ignore `.ce/` — governance subtrees under `.ce/` must remain trackable.
.ce/ce-events/spool/
